# Rust build artifacts
/target
/devops/tests/project/target
/modules/target
/examples/**/target/**

# Hot-reload runtime temp copies
modules/pill_standalone_temp/

# Host-generated project workspace member (created at runtime)
modules/optional/host_project_*/

# Generated build scratch (shipping bundle contents, build metadata).
#
# Ignore the CONTENTS rather than the directory itself: git never descends
# into an excluded directory, so a `build/` exclusion would make the
# negations below unreachable.
**/build/*

# ...except the shipping bundle crate skeleton, which is COMMITTED as a stub.
#
# `pill_standalone` declares `pill_shipping_bundle` as an optional path
# dependency. Cargo resolves every manifest in the workspace BEFORE it
# evaluates features, so a missing directory here breaks resolution for the
# whole workspace - including plain debug builds that never enable
# `static_project`, and including `cargo run -p editor`. `optional = true`
# means "do not compile it", not "do not look for it".
#
# The committed stub is deliberately project-agnostic. A shipping build
# overwrites both files through the generator's content-based writes, so a
# stable tree shows no diff; run `git checkout -- build/pill_shipping_bundle`
# to return to the neutral stub afterwards.
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/
build/pill_shipping_bundle/*
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/Cargo.toml
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/src/
build/pill_shipping_bundle/src/*
!build/pill_shipping_bundle/src/lib.rs

# Test infrastructure
devops/tests/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
.github/skills
.claude/


# Profiling and benchmark artifacts
graphify-out/
performance_benchmarks/cache/artifacts/

/devops/pill_lab/measurements/

# Local developer notes
local/

# Copilot instructions (generated)
.github/copilot-instructions.md

bin/
obj/

